## Exercise 1 — Type a Domain From Scratch
**Task:** Model a task tracker: a `Task` has an id, title, optional description, a status (todo/doing/done), creation date, and tags. Then write `createTask(title, tags?)` that produces a valid new task, and make `id` and `createdAt` impossible to modify after creation.
<details><summary>Hints</summary>
1. Status: a literal union, not `string`.
2. Impossible to modify → `readonly`.
3. `createTask` supplies defaults: status `"todo"`, empty tags, `crypto.randomUUID()`, `new Date()`.
</details>
**Solution:**
```ts
type Status = "todo" | "doing" | "done";
interface Task {
readonly id: string;
title: string;
description?: string;
status: Status;
readonly createdAt: Date;
tags: string[];
}
function createTask(title: string, tags: string[] = []): Task {
return {
id: crypto.randomUUID(),
title,
status: "todo",
createdAt: new Date(),
tags,
};
}
const t = createTask("Learn TS");
t.status = "doing";        // ✅ legal transition

